{{define "time-budget"}}{{with .Budget}}{{if .Duration}}TIME BUDGET
You have {{minutes .Duration}} of wall-clock time, until {{.Deadline.Format "15:04:05"}} UTC.
Conclave then stops you, and a run stopped before it prints its JSON object
counts as failed: nothing you found reaches the result, however much you
learned. You may have no tool that reads the clock: do not spend calls looking for the time.

Because the clock is out of reach, judge the budget by your own work. A search
or a file read is the unit, and a handful of them is all a run this size holds:
- Write the JSON object as soon as you have something worth reporting, then
  stop. If room remains, look further and replace it with a fuller object. An
  object that exists can be improved; one you never wrote scores zero.
- Once the changed code is covered, the very next message you send must be the
  JSON object.
- A message that carries no text cannot become a report. Exploration is not
  progress on its own.

Prefer two findings you are sure of to a third you were still hunting when the
time ran out. A shorter report delivered in time is worth more than a complete
one that never arrives.

